<http://data.silknow.org/object/596d2e37-9a3b-32ae-9c64-7ad3c8cc88e3/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress fabric of silk and metal thread.\n\nWoven silk and metal thread, plain weave ground and  binding.\nWarp: red silk, Z twist.\nWeft: red, white, dark green and light blue, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk, indeterminable twist. \nSeries of horizontal bands which metal thread ground  which may originally have been part of the border design on a larger object.  \nFrom the bottom up:\n[1] incomplete; three dark green rectangles\n[2] dark green spot alternating with a red spot\n[3] white 4-petalled flower-head between elongated dark green leaves\n[4] as [2]\n[5] deeper band with red flower, 2 pairs of dark green leaves and 2 light blue flowers\n[6] red cross alternating with dark green geometric motif."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/596d2e37-9a3b-32ae-9c64-7ad3c8cc88e3> .

